<h4><span class=3D"mw-headline" id=3D"Multi-Genre_Focus">Multi-Genre Focus<=
/span></h4>
<ol><li>For multi-genre combinations, the values are weighted with the firs=
t chosen genre being twice as important as the second one. Refer to the <a =
class=3D"mw-redirect" href=3D"https://gamedevtycoon.fandom.com/wiki/Review_=
Algorithm#Combination_study" title=3D"Review Algorithm">Review Algorithm</a=
> for more information on how the following values were calculated.</li></o=
l>
<p>The point of multi-genres is to eliminate a genre's requirements, giving=
 you more flexibility with what features to cram in. For example, Strategy/=
Adventure and Strategy/RPG has only 3 "+" fields and everything else is not=
 bound by rules, while if you'd be making Strategy or RPG, you'd have 6 "+"=
 fields and 1 "-" field to worry about, therefore, multi-genre gives you mo=
re creative freedom when you combine genres properly.
</p><p>The downside to using a multi-genre with less than 2 desired fields =
in a stage is that your game quality will not be increased as much as a mul=
ti-ged fields. <a class=3D"mw-redirect" href=3D"https://gamedevtycoon.fando=
m.com/wiki/Review_Algorithm#Design_decisions" title=3D"Review Algorithm">-s=
ource</a>
</p>
